WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.420
Return to our deployment case.

2
00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.980
Proposal A advertises a larger rack rating, but its thermal and transport

3
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:08.440
evidence doesn't identify the offered configuration.

4
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.360
Proposal B supplies revision-matched records, while the site team hasn't closed one

5
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:13.980
route constraint.

6
00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.140
Neither proposal is ready for unconditional acceptance.

7
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.620
The headline rating doesn't repair Proposal A's evidence gaps.

8
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.540
Proposal B may support a bounded next step, but only if the

9
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.960
unresolved route issue doesn't affect that activity.

10
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.240
A conditional decision must state what can proceed and what remains blocked.

11
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.280
Build the short decision record.

12
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.100
Name the missing evidence, its owner and the condition that would change

13
00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:37.580
the result.

14
00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.740
Compare the cost and feasibility of closing those gaps rather than treating

15
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.200
every unknown as equivalent.

16
00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:47.160
Pause and decide what you'd request first from each supplier and from

17
00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:47.760
the site team.

18
00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:52.280
A defensible choice may eventually favor either proposal, but it must follow

19
00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:55.560
the requirements and evidence, not the order of the marketing claims.

